2)Introduction to Linux
Linux is based on the UNIX operating system. 
UNIX is a powerful, multi-user, multitasking operating system originally developed in the 1970s at AT&T Bell Labs. 
It laid the foundation for many modern operating systems, including Linux.
a.Linux is free and open-source, accessible to everyone.
b.This promotes global collaboration and innovation.
c.Linux offers efficient performance and strong security.
d.It works well across many devices and industries.

3)Linux Commands?
Basic tools for utilizing the command line interface (CLI) to communicate with the operating system are Linux commands. Commonly used commands like:
ls – Lists contents of directories
cd – Changes the current directory
pwd – Displays the current directory path
cp, mv, rm – Used to copy, move, and delete files respectively
free – Shows memory usage
df – Checks disk space usage
top – Monitors running processes
netstat, ifconfig, ping – Help monitor and troubleshoot network connections

